  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Apple chutney is what happens to a glut of autumn apples,  cooked with brown sugar, malt vinegar, and spices until thick, dark, and warmly flavoured. It works alongside a ploughman's lunch, in cheese toasties, with cold pork, and on a charcuterie board. Makes about four 300 g jars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
